2. Complete partitioning of state array to enable parallel read-modify-write operations
3. Maintained full loop unrolling to maximize parallelism
4. Preserved original function signatures and logic

This configuration reduces memory access bottlenecks while maintaining maximum operation parallelism, potentially enabling all 16 XOR operations to execute in parallel in a single cycle.
